{"name":"New Forest","hex":"#47514d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"New Forest","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large area, forest, and national park in Wiltshire and Hampshire, southern England.","A local government district in Hampshire, created in 1974."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/New_Forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"New Forest","blocks":[{"text":"The New Forest is one of the largest remaining tracts of unenclosed pasture land, heathland and forest in Southern England, covering southwest Hampshire and southeast Wiltshire. It was proclaimed a royal forest by William the Conqueror, featuring in Domesday Book."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Beech_trees_in_Mallard_Wood%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_779513.jpg/330px-Beech_trees_in_Mallard_Wood%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_779513.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Forest","wikidata":"Q277755"},{"title":"New Forest (constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"New Forest was a county constituency in south-west Hampshire which elected one Member of Parliament (MP) to the House of Commons of the Parliament of the United Kingdom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/NewForest1983Constituency.svg/330px-NewForest1983Constituency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Forest_(constituency)","wikidata":"Q7007620"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Beaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaulieu_Mill_Pond%2C_New_Forest%2C_UK_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Royal.Forests.1327.1336.selected.jpg/500px-Royal.Forests.1327.1336.selected.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Royal.Forests.1327.1336.selected.jpg/1280px-Royal.Forests.1327.1336.selected.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/